# RR24a explicit shared duplicate-key compatibility

Migrations require the final value at the first decoded-key insertion position, while RR01 intentionally rejects duplicates. Add a separate opt-in DuplicateKeys::LastWins entry through parse_with_duplicate_keys; existing parse still delegates Reject. The same preflight, syntax validator, builder and materializer remain authoritative. A BTreeMap indexes decoded keys, replacing only the previous ordered member value. Raw input retains every byte, original numeric lexemes remain tokens, and ordinary private-marker objects remain objects. All physical occurrences consume key/value/scalar/depth limits before collapse, including discarded malformed or oversized values. No second parser or key-name guessing is introduced.

All sixteen cases pass: eleven original strict-parser and five new compatibility cases. Manual ordered/literal oracles cover nested and escaped-equivalent duplicates, overwritten containers and invalid data, private marker keys, numeric spelling, exact/-1 physical budgets, raw preservation and cancellation. The first root attempt failed to compile an inferred BTreeMap index; adding an explicit String/usize annotation fixed it before any test ran. Failed capture remains retained. rr24a-02 passes all tests, scoped formatting and all-target Clippy. rr24a-03 adds only README API discoverability with identical tested Rust source; no tests were replayed for that documentation-only change. State patches retain exact earlier source hashes.

Independent review accepted the final source, annotation and documentation. The old strict behavior is deliberate, not relabeled a bug. This prerequisite is separately reviewed from RR24 adoption, which pins six exact crate blobs. No dependency or registry baseline changes, default-policy weakening, native capacity, UI or product acceptance is claimed.

Implementation commit: `d16f6436ec5c133a7b5819c7e4198b57fe88f0e8`. [Executed and committed inputs](executed-source-binding.json), [independent review](independent-review.json), [captures](captures/). Status: **LOCALLY_VERIFIED_BOUNDED / NOT_ACCEPTED**. No new registry tuple. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify; never merge into feature or temporary snapshot bases. Existing holds remain held.
